From f3cc6f5c71622c5ea857c39c780618227d8a6e4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiBr <me@nvme0n1p.dev>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 13:35:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/57] Z 6III: a CFexpress card -- NVMe on PCIe port 2,
 formatted by the camera

-machine cfexpress=on puts ../z9-qemu's PCIe port-2 adapter
(nikon-z9-pcie.h, imported with deb3a75) in front of the board: QEMU's
DesignWare host behind DBI 0x1a800000, the unrolled iATU and the CPU
aperture at 0x600000000, the port's link wrappers at 0x17b00000 and its
legacy interrupt on INTID 0x95 (EXS_PCIE10_PCIE_MISC). The card is an
NVMe device on that bus:

  -drive if=none,id=cf,file=<image>,format=raw
  -device nvme,drive=cf,serial=<s>,bus=dw-pcie,addr=0

What the board adds:

  - the slot's detect: EXS +0x044 bit 1 (index 2 * 2 + 13 of the EXS
    offset table, sub_4028C1CC), set while a card is configured
    (nikon-z63-usb.h). DECLARED: present means bit 1;
  - the adapter's DMA view: the board's DRAM at 0xa00000000 (the state
    now carries z63_dram, which import_z9lab.py substitutes for
    MACHINE(s)->ram in nikon-z9-pcie.h as well as in the lab) and
    BUFFER_EXT aliased where the Z 9 aliases its image banks
    (pcie-image-ram-dma-input stays refused);
  - the link wrappers' page in the z9lab range, for cfexpress only;
  - ../z9-qemu's designware.c fix: an iATU limit takes the base's high
    bits, and size 0 disables the window.

With a blank 8 GiB image the camera shows [ For ] (card present, not
formatted); SETUP > Format memory card > CFexpress/XQD > Yes formats it
("Format complete"), and live view then counts 867 shots. The card
holds what the camera wrote: an MBR with one FAT32 (LBA) partition at
LBA 63 and a boot sector "NIKON5.0", label "NIKON Z6_3".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
